            <ArticleTitle>Preoperative preparatory program has no effect on morbidly obese patients undergoing a Lap-Band operation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>250-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">A preoperative preparatory program may help morbidly obese patients cope with postoperative pain and vomiting, and reduce length of nursing care.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A preoperative preparatory program was given to randomly selected morbidly obese women about to undergo a Lap-Band stomach reduction operation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Statistical testing of the results of the program against a control group of patients who did not receive the program revealed beneficial differences between the two groups in terms of postoperative pain, analgesic use, postoperative vomiting, and duration of nursing care.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The differences were not statistically significant, although the reaction of patients who received the program was positive.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
